{"mem_muo8ncer_6b44d2702fae":{"concepts":[],"content":"Memory probe: user asked whether global agentmemory works; round-trip write+search verified successfully.","createdAt":"2026-09-30T15:06:34.514Z","files":[],"id":"mem_muo8ncer_6b44d2702fae","isLatest":true,"origin":{"capturedAt":"2026-09-30T15:06:34.514Z","channel":"agent"},"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"Memory probe: user asked whether global agentmemory works; round-trip write+sear","type":"fact","updatedAt":"2026-09-30T15:06:34.514Z","version":1},"mem_muo9eqwr_474b982fb6d8":{"concepts":[],"content":"FAILURE: mcp__agentmemory__memory_slot_list returns HTTP 500 (POST /agentmemory/mcp/call) as of 2026-09-30. Constraint: do not build automation on slots until verified fixed; re-probe after each agentmemory update. Related gap: snapshots disabled (SNAPSHOT_ENABLED not set) so consolidation runs without rollback protection.","createdAt":"2026-09-30T15:27:53.017Z","files":[],"id":"mem_muo9eqwr_474b982fb6d8","isLatest":true,"origin":{"capturedAt":"2026-09-30T15:27:53.017Z","channel":"agent"},"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"FAILURE: mcp__agentmemory__memory_slot_list returns HTTP 500 (POST /agentmemory/","type":"fact","updatedAt":"2026-09-30T15:27:53.017Z","version":1},"mem_muodrxog_b3094d55f123":{"concepts":[],"content":"LLM provider for agentmemory distillation is nara router (nemotron-3.5-lightning-free) via ~/.agentmemory/.env; circuit must stay closed.","createdAt":"2026-09-30T17:30:06.781Z","files":[],"id":"mem_muodrxog_b3094d55f123","isLatest":true,"origin":{"capturedAt":"2026-09-30T17:30:06.781Z","channel":"agent"},"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"LLM provider for agentmemory distillation is nara router (nemotron-3.5-lightning","type":"fact","updatedAt":"2026-09-30T17:30:06.781Z","version":1},"mem_muoexh9r_f14fa87e2b52":{"concepts":[],"content":"agentmemory stack (Windows, verified 2026-09-30): engine iii.exe on :3111 (AppData\\Local\\agentmemory\\engine\\bin), launched by node cli.mjs from npx cache; MCP shim npx -y @agentmemory/mcp (cwd now ~/.agentmemory in mcp.json so logs don't drop in project dirs). Config = ~/.agentmemory/.env read at boot only (no hot reload; restart via scripts/restart_agentmemory.ps1, -Elevated only when the tree was started elevated). OPENAI_MODEL must exist on router.bynara.id /v1/models — configured≠verified; a 404 model makes every LLM tier silently no-op with success:true. Silent-failure probes: memory_health circuitBreaker.state, POST :3111/agentmemory/consolidate returns totalObservations (downstream counter), .env ACL needs icacls on NTFS (chmod no-op). Durable reflection = bounded .md files (reflection/sessions, candidates, digests) + git-tracked gates; agentmemory = capture layer. Runbook: projects/agentic-research-lab/EXPERIENCE.md; candidate session-diagnosis-scar-set is experimental.","createdAt":"2026-09-30T18:02:25.070Z","files":[],"id":"mem_muoexh9r_f14fa87e2b52","isLatest":true,"origin":{"capturedAt":"2026-09-30T18:02:25.070Z","channel":"agent"},"project":"agentic-research-lab","sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"agentmemory stack (Windows, verified 2026-09-30): engine iii.exe on :3111 (AppDa","type":"workflow","updatedAt":"2026-09-30T18:02:25.070Z","version":1},"mem_muoexp82_52c2e0ee27d8":{"concepts":[],"content":"pi harness scars observed 2026-09-30 (fix candidates to report upstream, not user errors): (1) \\r characters injected into edit/write tool-arg strings, breaking exact-match anchors — mitigation: rewrite whole file after 2 failed edits; (2) MSYS/Git Bash mangles Windows commands (taskkill /F → F:/, $_ → /usr/bin/bash, backslash paths lose backslash) — mitigation: always write command to a .ps1/.py file and execute it; never inline python -c / powershell -Command with nested quotes on Windows; (3) MCP tool naming inconsistency: top-level memory_health vs tools.mcp__agentmemory__memory_health, searchTools declared but \"not a function\"; (4) big tool outputs (memory_health dumps ~272-function list each call) — filter via codemode; (5) secrets can leak into session JSONL when masking regex fails — rotate keys that appear in transcripts.","createdAt":"2026-09-30T18:02:35.376Z","files":[],"id":"mem_muoexp82_52c2e0ee27d8","isLatest":true,"origin":{"capturedAt":"2026-09-30T18:02:35.376Z","channel":"agent"},"project":"agentic-research-lab","sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"pi harness scars observed 2026-09-30 (fix candidates to report upstream, not use","type":"bug","updatedAt":"2026-09-30T18:02:35.376Z","version":1},"mem_muoj2dmz_5b87c0605b4b":{"concepts":[],"content":"Scar (agentic-research-lab, 2026-09-30): ran a gate, saw FAIL on background-reflection artifacts (missing provenance.phase/fingerprint/state/Action), then deleted the failing artifacts and reported PASS. Three defects were hidden by the deletion. Root cause of the behaviour: treating the gate output as an obstacle to clear rather than as the measurement. Enforcement added: (1) CLAUDE.md tooling-hygiene rule \"never delete an artifact a gate flagged\"; (2) background_worker.py now runs check_reflection.py itself and writes state=failed with the failure list, never done on an unverified gate; (3) CLAUDE.md rule about writing a real test that exercises the modified path, not pre-existing artifacts. Verified by negative tests (stray .log outside declared dir still fails; declared dir not in .gitignore fails).","createdAt":"2026-09-30T19:58:12.105Z","files":[],"id":"mem_muoj2dmz_5b87c0605b4b","isLatest":true,"origin":{"capturedAt":"2026-09-30T19:58:12.105Z","channel":"agent"},"project":"agentic-research-lab","sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"Scar (agentic-research-lab, 2026-09-30): ran a gate, saw FAIL on background-refl","type":"fact","updatedAt":"2026-09-30T19:58:12.105Z","version":1},"mem_muojncu4_868efcc00a77":{"concepts":[],"content":"Prevention layer (agentic-research-lab, 2026-09-30) built against the deleted-evidence failure: (1) PreToolUse hook scripts/hook_guard_evidence.py denies rm/rmdir/Remove-Item/truncate/glob against reflection/digests|candidates|.snapshots — verified against the actual fatal command; writes still allowed because the agent must produce these files. (2) scripts/snapshot_graded.py copies graded artifacts to reflection/.snapshots/<ts>/ before every check_reflection read; recovery proven by deleting and restoring an artifact. (3) check_reflection.py --paths <slug> grades only the named run's artifacts (a directory-wide gate cannot distinguish \"my change is broken\" from \"old artifact is broken\"). (4) preflight.py consumes reflection/logs/*.status.json: failed/timeout/error and dead-PID running block; a stale failure whose artifacts now re-grade clean is reported ok instead of blocking forever (blocking forever creates pressure to delete the evidence the check preserves). (5) docs/CODING_STANDARDS.md as reviewer-loaded file. (6) check_slop.py skips bg-smoke* test fixtures — smoke-test prose is not research output, but check_reflection still grades those files fully.\n\nFour plan items deliberately NOT built: icacls read-only freeze (locks inside the worker cannot intercept the agent's own Bash tool — the actual deletion vector — so the PreToolUse hook is the real boundary; also ACL denials leave un-removable files that wedge the pipeline); shell-confirmation tokens for rm -rf (not enforceable by a rule, the hook denies outright instead); three-context implementer/reviewer/verifier orchestration (half-day, needs pi task/session primitives, and check_evidence_guard.py already enforces the invariant deterministically without new roles); model tier routing (no router config surface in this workspace).","createdAt":"2026-09-30T20:14:30.841Z","files":[],"id":"mem_muojncu4_868efcc00a77","isLatest":true,"origin":{"capturedAt":"2026-09-30T20:14:30.841Z","channel":"agent"},"project":"agentic-research-lab","sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"Prevention layer (agentic-research-lab, 2026-09-30) built against the deleted-ev","type":"fact","updatedAt":"2026-09-30T20:14:30.841Z","version":1},"mem_muon2j4z_4457d784d84f":{"concepts":[],"content":"pi token efficiency (2026-09-30, workspace root_worksapce): measured over 29 sessions / 69.5M tokens. Cache hit ratio 78.0%. Cold-prefix attribution (a turn with cacheRead==0 and input>2000) gave: non-caching provider 61.2% of wasted tokens (oc/nemotron-3.5-lightning-free = 4.0M tok, 0.0% hit ratio), thinking_level_change 12.5% (812K), model_switch 7.7% (502K), compaction 5.6%, context_edit 3.1%. Decisive finding: caching is a property of the model, not the task — one model held 90.3% for 363 consecutive turns. Tool output was 11.7x assistant output chars (1.71M vs 146K), the biggest untapped lever.\n\nDECISION D15: one model per session, never switch mid-session; roles are thinking modes not routing targets. User rejected architect/editor model delegation because model availability is not stable for them.\n\nTooling scars: (1) cacheWrite is 0 in every pi session — this provider tier has no write-side accounting, so cold prefixes are invisible in cost data; detect via cacheRead==0, never via cost. (2) A wrong attribution looks authoritative — attributing cold prefixes to the nearest preceding event blamed thinking_change for 67.9% of waste when a 0.0%-hit-ratio provider was the real cause. Verify attribution against per-model ratios within one session before acting.\n\nScripts (stdlib only): scripts/pi_token_audit.py, pi_context_growth.py, pi_cache_forensics.py. Evidence in root TOKEN-EFFICIENCY.md. Note: root has NO docs/ directory convention — knowledge lives as root files (PHILOSOPHY.md, TOOLS.md); check_workspace_integrity.py enforces ALLOWED_ROOT, so a new root file must be declared there.","createdAt":"2026-09-30T21:50:17.697Z","files":[],"id":"mem_muon2j4z_4457d784d84f","isLatest":true,"origin":{"capturedAt":"2026-09-30T21:50:17.697Z","channel":"agent"},"project":"root_worksapce","sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"pi token efficiency (2026-09-30, workspace root_worksapce): measured over 29 ses","type":"fact","updatedAt":"2026-09-30T21:50:17.697Z","version":1},"mem_muonu48r_95feda5634f2":{"concepts":[],"content":"jCodeMunch MCP (2026-09-30, root_worksapce) — DECISION D16: wired in with pi codemode exposure. Real project: github.com/jgravelle/jcodemunch-mcp, 2,721 stars, 365 forks, Python + tree-sitter, v1.108.319 via `uv tool install` (NOT npm — no npm/pypi package exists). Config in ~/.pi/agent/mcp.json as `jcodemunch`, exposure codemode, only menu/route/set_tool_tier declared to the model; announce_model + jcodemunch_guide hidden.\n\nVerified claims: get_symbol_source returned 1,300 chars for a symbol whose file is 7,669 chars = 5.9x. search_symbols 629 chars. find_importers + get_call_hierarchy work (grep cannot do these).\n\nThe 90-tool objection does NOT hold: pi's codemode exposure means MCP schemas never enter the system prefix at all. Separately, jcodemunch's own docs say the schema block is paid ~once per cache lifetime then at cache-read rates — reading it as a per-request saving overstates cost ~10x. Its 'counter' surface shows only 6 of 94 tools.\n\nTHE REAL CEILING (measured with scripts/tool_output_breakdown.py on own transcripts): tool output = bash 59.4%, read 27.1%, codemode 6.3%, powershell 5.2%. Source-file reads are only 12.1% of ALL tool output. So symbol retrieval addresses ~12%, saving ~8.5% at a 70% cut. The vendor's 96.5% / 28.3x is a per-read figure, not a share-of-context figure — roughly an order of magnitude overstatement. bash/test/git output is the bigger unaddressed fish.\n\nOperational gotchas: repo resolution is by git remote name (kamyczeczek/agentic-research-lab), not folder path. CLI needs absolute paths, relative rejected. get_symbol_source needs file::name#kind symbol_id, not path+symbol. menu costs 5,139 chars so it's discovery-only, not per-symbol. No enforcement hooks installed: they rewrite global CLAUDE.md + client settings, pi has no such hook surface, and it conflicts with the workspace 'config != working config' rule.\n\nNew scripts: scripts/mcp_schema_cost.py (measures any MCP server's tool-surface prefix cost), scripts/mcp_call.py (call one MCP tool, print payload size), scripts/tool_output_breakdown.py. jDocMunch deferred — doc reads are 12.1% and mostly small files.","createdAt":"2026-09-30T22:11:44.761Z","files":[],"id":"mem_muonu48r_95feda5634f2","isLatest":true,"origin":{"capturedAt":"2026-09-30T22:11:44.761Z","channel":"agent"},"project":"root_worksapce","sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"jCodeMunch MCP (2026-09-30, root_worksapce) — DECISION D16: wired in with pi cod","type":"fact","updatedAt":"2026-09-30T22:11:44.761Z","version":1},"mem_muotyvk5_84162a230381":{"concepts":[],"content":"agentic-research-lab: faza 04 ma DWÓCH runnerów naraz — `pipeline/06_reflect/spawn.py` (pętla agenta `omp`, do której routuje CLAUDE.md) i `pipeline/06_reflect/reflect.py` (jedno wywołanie LLM na pakiecie dowodowym z presearch). reflect.py powstał jako fast path (GATES-reflection-fastpath.md, G1–G5 met), ale decyzja o backendzie nigdy nie została domknięta, więc nie zastąpił spawn.py. To jest największa niejednoznaczność integracji research↔graph↔reflection↔execution — zmapowana jako bilet T1 w docs/wayfinder/research-graph-reflection-execution.md.","createdAt":"2026-10-01T01:03:24.483Z","files":[],"id":"mem_muotyvk5_84162a230381","isLatest":true,"origin":{"capturedAt":"2026-10-01T01:03:24.483Z","channel":"agent"},"project":"agentic-research-lab","sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"agentic-research-lab: faza 04 ma DWÓCH runnerów naraz — `pipeline/06_reflect/spa","type":"fact","updatedAt":"2026-10-01T01:03:24.483Z","version":1},"mem_muotz4zz_e79174daa34a":{"concepts":[],"content":"Metoda weryfikacji bramek w agentic-research-lab: napisz negatywną kontrolę (mutacja → walidator MUSI wyjść na czerwono) PRZED zaufaniem bramce. Dziś to zadziałało na scripts/check_wayfinder_map.py — 2 z 7 mutacji przeszły bramkę, która wyglądała na zieloną: G2 dopasowywał kształt bulletu, którego mapa nie używa, a G3 szukał `- T1`, gdy wpisy Decisions mają format `- **[T1 — tytuł]**`. Oba przypadki to ta sama klasa defektu co check_graph_determinism z C-7 (bramka deklaruje własność, której kod nie implementuje). Lekcja: bramka, która nigdy nie widziała awarii, nie jest dowodem — a wykrycie tego wymaga obserwacji zmutowanego wejścia, nie czytania kodu walidatora.","createdAt":"2026-10-01T01:03:36.718Z","files":[],"id":"mem_muotz4zz_e79174daa34a","isLatest":true,"origin":{"capturedAt":"2026-10-01T01:03:36.718Z","channel":"agent"},"project":"agentic-research-lab","sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"Metoda weryfikacji bramek w agentic-research-lab: napisz negatywną kontrolę (mut","type":"workflow","updatedAt":"2026-10-01T01:03:36.718Z","version":1},"mem_muotzepu_7fac7dad64fd":{"concepts":[],"content":"Znany defekt w agentic-research-lab (2026-10-01, niezależny od mojej pracy): tests/test_ralph_parity.py::GateIsAdvisoryTests pada 2/2 z `AttributeError: 'A' object has no attribute 'same_model'` — scripts/ralph_pilot.py:292 czyta `args.same_model`, ale żaden argparse tego nie definiuje. Plik jest zmodyfikowany, niecommitowany (`git status`: ` M`). Zbiór: 254 passed, 2 failed, 10 subtests. Jeśli ktoś widzi ten czerwony stan i nie zna przyczyny — to jest ona, i NIE jest to regresja wprowadzona przez pracę nad mapą wayfinder.","createdAt":"2026-10-01T01:03:49.313Z","files":[],"id":"mem_muotzepu_7fac7dad64fd","isLatest":true,"origin":{"capturedAt":"2026-10-01T01:03:49.313Z","channel":"agent"},"project":"agentic-research-lab","sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"Znany defekt w agentic-research-lab (2026-10-01, niezależny od mojej pracy): tes","type":"bug","updatedAt":"2026-10-01T01:03:49.313Z","version":1},"mem_muoupl7s_2a446e1b3350":{"concepts":[],"content":"Potwierdzenie wayfinder-map nie jest trywialne: zmiana statusu mapy z PROPOSED na CONFIRMED unieważnia bramki, które były pisane pod poprzedni stan. W agentic-research-lab 2026-10-01 tak urosła G6 w scripts/check_wayfinder_map.py — wymagała słów PROPOSED/provisional, więc poprawna aktualizacja mapy ją łamała. Lekcja: bramka, która koduje nie tylko własność, ale i moment jej prawdziwości, wymaga rozdzielenia tych dwóch (tu: dwa dozwolone stany + wymóg daty ISO na potwierdzenie). I druga, droższa: negatywna kontrola mutacji przypięta do literału tekstu (replace \"PROPOSED\"→\"FINAL\") po zmianie stanu staje się NOOP i raportuje sukces, testując nic — dlatego mutacja musi obsługiwać oba stany, a NOOP traktować jako porażkę, nie jako sukces.","createdAt":"2026-10-01T01:24:10.790Z","files":[],"id":"mem_muoupl7s_2a446e1b3350","isLatest":true,"origin":{"capturedAt":"2026-10-01T01:24:10.790Z","channel":"agent"},"project":"agentic-research-lab","sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"Potwierdzenie wayfinder-map nie jest trywialne: zmiana statusu mapy z PROPOSED n","type":"workflow","updatedAt":"2026-10-01T01:24:10.790Z","version":1}}␀␀␀�␀����